#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 355 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Shifts an envelope horizontally in time: adds the given
time-shift value (in milliseconds) to all time values of the envelope.
A positive shift delays the envelope \, a negative shift moves it earlier.
The shape of the envelope is not affected — only its position in time.;
#X text 240 168 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 193 • Aligning an envelope to a specific moment — moving
an envelope forward or backward in time so that its key points (for
example \, its peak) coincide with the desired moment in a sequence
or a recorded performance.;
#X text 250 263 • Layering delayed envelopes — creating rhythmic or
spatial effects by combining the same envelope with a shifted copy
of itself \, for example a short delay between two notes or between
two amplitude shapes.;
#X text 250 333 • Real-time timing control — changing the offset of
an envelope in real time by linking the shift to a knob \, an LFO \,
or a performance parameter such as key velocity or mod wheel \, to
obtain groovy or expressive timing variations.;
